# Backend build context (docker build ... backend).
#
# Without this file, every build sends about 1.5 GB to the daemon — models/ is
# 1.2 GB and data/ is 314 MB — and, much worse, SECRETS: backend/.env may contain
# an OpenRouter Management Key and the Postgres password, data/secret.key is the
# JWT signing secret, and data/openrouter.key is the shared inference key. The
# Dockerfile would not currently copy them, but a file excluded from the context
# cannot accidentally enter a layer later when somebody adds another COPY.

# --- Secrets and local configuration: never include in the context ---
# Covers .env, .env.production, and backup names such as .env.production.bak.
.env*

# --- Runtime data: databases, keys, and user documents ---
data/

# --- PII model: 1.2 GB, mounted at runtime (see Dockerfile) ---
# IMPORTANT: this is `models/`, NOT `**/models/`. In .dockerignore, a pattern
# without ** applies only at the context root, which is exactly what we need:
# app/engine/models/signature_yolo11n.onnx (10.6 MB, the OCR signature/stamp
# detector) is versioned inside app/ and MUST enter the image. With `**/models/`
# it disappeared and OCR silently lost signature detection.
models/

# --- Local virtual environment and bytecode ---
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# --- Not needed in the backend image ---
# Suites run manually from the repository with their fixtures and fake
# OpenRouter server: 6 MB that the container does not need.
tests/
# Separate image: docker build -t blockingbear-sandbox:1 backend/sandbox
# (it has a different context, so this exclusion does not affect it).
sandbox/
# Used only to regenerate test documents, not to run the application.
requirements-dev.txt

# --- Meta ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
